My First Ascension ever! And I managed to pull it off with a Tourist! :)
I was playing on same server as Alan Schwartz who posted YAAP couple 
days ago (and beat me to first ascension score on the server. At least I 
beat him in score :)). This was in fact, my first game where I even got 
to Gehennom, or saw the Castle, or Medusa... (For certain values of 
seeing the Medusa, blindfolded with ESP only)

Here's the story of Viila the Rambler...

Beginning of the game was absolutely plagued with lack of ID and Holy 
Water. I didn't get an altar until some levels above Medusa. Minetown 
was bones file with displaced priest, so first time I got to play 
protection racket was priest of Moloch in VoD. Got 8 points worth of 
priestly AC from him initially, and another point later. I read total of 
7 uncursed and 10 blessed Scrolls of ID before I finally got a full 
inventory ID with the 11th.

The whole game was very odd with RNG results. 1/10 odds seemed to happen 
9 times out of 10. I got a blessed magic lamp from Minetown which 
proceeded to yeild hostile djinni. Few levels later I found another 
magic lamp. I found 2 bags of holding before Sokoban (got AoR from 
there). A Wand of Wishing from Sokoban, with 3 charges. In total, I 
found 5 magic lamps in the whole game! I wasted two wishes for Magicbane 
since my god wasn't forthcoming, but never got the darned thing. Only 
artifact weapon was the Giantslayer (from saccing 50+ or so monsters) 
which is next to useless. Went most of the game with unicorn horn, then 
period with thrice enchanted runed dagger (for Magicbane practice), and 
finally did Gehennom wielding a thrice enchanted silver sabre (lost 
enchantments to disenchanter. I didn't get message, so I thought I was 
fine, but after ID'ing the sabre it was +0!) which was then enchanted to 
+6 before dealing with Rodney.

Equipment when entering the valley was:
+5 GDSM, +4 hawaiian shirt, +0 SoReflection, +4 GoPower, +0 Elvish 
Cloak, +1 iron boots, +1 iron helm. I wished for speed boots only right 
before meeting Rodney. I think I was a bit too cautious in spending 
wishes. Oh well. I didn't have a way to fireproof my cloak, so I entered 
Gehennom amusingly with 4 cloaks. By the time I had the Amulet, I had 
gone through 3 of them. :P

Killed Orcus and Rodney on the way down with a rubber chicken. I also 
upgraded Orcus's ghost town into a fine arts museum with lot's of 
statues on exhibit. I used the dig through floor, come up stairs method 
to kill each of the big Demons. (Except Yeenoghu, which someone had 
summoned up to Valley of Death).

After I killed Rodney, I made one (potentially serious) plunder. I had 
taken my =oTC off, and then read a cursed ?oT to level teleport down to 
vibrating square. Instead, I ended up on dlvl 14! Oops. Thankfully, I 
had another cursed scroll to teleport to VoD, and then made one more 
using some unholy water to get down to the bottom.

Made the invocation, and then hacked path through the graveyard 
(literally) with stealth assist. The priests died easily enough and the 
High Priest became familiar with my /oD. I then wished for a cursed 
potion of Gain Level and made my escape with the amulet.

The way up would theoretically be swift with path made ready and 
abundant teleportation capabilities... Suffice to say that I passed 
through Orcus Town three times and Yeenoghu's swamp freaking 8 or 9 
times... It seems the RNG racked up all the downfalls into that one 
excruciatingly painfull see-saw through few levels in Gehennom. Above 
those it was smooth sailing, and I don't think it activated even once in 
the dungeon proper. Rodney didn't make any appearances in person, which 
is just as well. He did summon nasties few times, but each time I either 
teleported away, or teleported some of them away and ran.

In Plane of Earth, I made the mistake of not looking at my /oD cursing 
status, and it blew up in my face when I was going to kill Double 
Trouble Rodney. Ouch. Thankfully, I had a spare. Always bring spares 
seems to be a good maxim for NetHack ;)

The elemental planes were boring. By this time I was worse than War 
incarnate. I was the whole Apocalypse all in one! 310 hps, AC -33, and 
(natural) str 18/12, Dx 18, Co 18, int 14, wi 17, ch 18. (I had pretty 
much those stats right after Valley of Dead already, except AC: -29, 250 
hp and less int&wis)

Another potential plunder. Upon arriving to Astral Plane, I forgot to 
swap AoMB back to AoLS (had had 2 of them before even Medusa, without 
wishing any, 3rd from Vlad). Though, it turned out that I didn't need it 
anyway. During my way to hack into first temple, I never got even below 
200 hps. After finding it was Blind Io's, I wished for a cockatrice 
corpse and proceeded to whack my way to the middle temple with it. It 
was the right one, and after brief singing of heavenly choir, I had 
achieved Demigodhood!

In Astral Plane, I also tried out the jumping boots, which worked ok 
after a few false starts. But not sure if they were beneficial over the 
speed boots. I had quaffed a !oSpeed, so I wasn't really any slower (at 
least for a while), but dunno.

I was really quite too much of a pack-rat. I had hard time keeping 
unburdened even with BoH. And I spent probably half the game with 
burdened status total (Mostly above gehennom, though I had the YAFM 
moment when I entered Gehennom. The game played how terrible place it 
is, and then majestically said "Do you want to enter? Y. So be it. You 
fall down the stairs.")

In the end, I used a solution to keep with me two BoHs. One with my 
immediate supplies, and another with my spares and long term supplies. 
Go down a level, drop the store bag on Elbereth, find downstairs, dig 
path to upstairs, retrieve bag, go down a level and repeat.

I don't think there was any staircase in the whole dungeon which I 
hadn't fallen down at least once, except maybe the dlvl 1 -> dlvl 2 
stairs...

